  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Complete selected distance calculation, built-in producer/list consumer and scoped value application bodies; existing STMG loader and special-binding owner reused.",
    "direct": "The enabled first built-in input reads the ray distance field, selects binding list 1, walks packed ID/type rows and performs exact namespace/key lookup. A retained override suppresses scoped application. The supplied float and 48-byte object scope enter the original value-application path. The component rebuild writes distance into its retained ray-array rows; its preparation routine selects a row from that same base/stride and passes that exact pointer into the built-in updater. This is explicit caller/operand transport, not a shared-offset inference. Original transition processing visits both manager lists, computes progress or selects the final target, snapshots retained user pointers and invokes their value/completion virtual callback. The selected parameter transition receiver clears its retained transition on completion and re-enters scoped value application with the delivered float. Full manager creation, clock advancement and all curve/filter modes remain unexecuted by the immediate-value cohorts. An immediate changed scoped value dispatches old/new floats, scope and the packed control key through each retained subscriber virtual callback slot. Scope creation can migrate matching wildcard subscribers from the default list to a scoped list; notification counters and mutation flags govern traversal/restart. This is separate from the slot-zero observer dispatch.",
    "conditional": "Distance is a float32 norm of float32 converted double-coordinate differences, optionally recalculated from a retained probe, divided by listener/source scaling under the selected component comparison. This is an internal distance-derived quantity, not a guaranteed raw-world meter distance. Stored binding admission, allocation, scope construction and producer scheduling remain conditions. Nonzero default transition policy can enter a retained transition helper rather than immediate value notification. Complete time-varying smoothing and target migration generations are not executed by this static proof.",
    "unresolved": "Actual game emitter/listener/probe objects, full scoped notification/destruction lifetime, current physical bank selection and audibility. Approximate historical SDK symbol matches alone are not naming proof."
  },
